  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Aminobenzoic acid and HepG2, mediated through the enzyme Glucose-1-phosphate thymidylyltransferase. This enzyme is targeted by two distinct compounds: Aminobenzoic acid and 2-(3-Ethenyl-4-pyridinyl)ethanol, both of which are linked to the cell line HepG2. The scores for these relationships, while not perfectly aligned, indicate a moderate level of confidence in the interaction between Aminobenzoic acid and HepG2 through this enzymatic pathway. The presence of multiple targets in the pathway suggests that Aminobenzoic acid may exert its effects by modulating the activity of Glucose-1-phosphate thymidylyltransferase, which in turn influences HepG2 cell behavior. The integration of these findings highlights the importance of enzyme-target interactions in understanding the biological effects of compounds on cancer cell lines like HepG2."
